# Bulk data stays out. Trip files are gigabytes and they already live in the
# bucket, and a zip of the repository belongs beside it, never inside it. We
# keep code in here, plus the small fixtures under data/ that the tests need:
# Parquet and zip files are excluded everywhere, and the one negation below
# lets Parquet fixtures whose names start with fixture_ back in.
*.parquet
*.zip
!data/fixture_*

# Secrets. Never commit one. Deleting it in a later commit does not remove it
# from the history, and a leaked token stays usable until you rotate it, so
# rotate it first. These patterns come after the negation above, so they win
# everywhere, data/ included.
.env
*.pem
*key*.json
service-account*.json

# Notebook checkpoints and tool caches
.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Environments and editors
.venv/
venv/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
